  Guarantees the same results given the same `seed` independent of how many
  times the function is called, and independent of global seed settings (e.g.
  `tf.random.set_seed`).

  Example usage:

  >>> image = np.array([[[1], [2]], [[3], [4]]])
  >>> seed = (2, 3)
